# Cloudflare Tunnel connector token for the public demo (deploy/docker-compose.demo.yml).
# Copy to `cloudflared.env` and fill in the real token; NEVER commit the filled file
# (deploy/.gitignore ignores *.env). Use with:
#   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.demo.yml --env-file deploy/cloudflared.env up -d
#
# The token is the connector credential from a Cloudflare Zero Trust "Named Tunnel"
# (Access > Tunnels > your tunnel > Install connector). It both authenticates the
# connector and carries its routing config, so it is the ONLY secret needed here —
# there is no tierd API token (the demo is loopback-only + read-only, #429).
# Treat it as a secret: it grants ingress to your tunnel. Keep the file mode 0600.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
